## Proxy Pattern

## Intent

Provide a surrogate that controls access to the real object, adding behaviour (caching, logging, validation, access control) transparently.

## JavaScript Proxy Object

```typescript
const user = { name: 'Aaron', role: 'admin', salary: 95000 };

// Access control proxy
const restrictedUser = new Proxy(user, {
  get(target, prop) {
    if (prop === 'salary') throw new Error('Access denied: salary is confidential');
    return Reflect.get(target, prop);
  },
  set(target, prop, value) {
    if (prop === 'role') throw new Error('Role is immutable');
    return Reflect.set(target, prop, value);
  },
});

console.log(restrictedUser.name); // 'Aaron'
console.log(restrictedUser.salary); // throws: Access denied
restrictedUser.role = 'user'; // throws: Role is immutable
```

## Validation Proxy

```typescript
function createValidated<T extends object>(target: T, validators: Partial<Record<keyof T, (v: any) => boolean>>): T {
  return new Proxy(target, {
    set(obj, prop, value) {
      const validate = validators[prop as keyof T];
      if (validate && !validate(value)) {
        throw new Error(`Invalid value for ${String(prop)}: ${value}`);
      }
      return Reflect.set(obj, prop, value);
    },
  });
}

const product = createValidated(
  { name: '', price: 0 },
  { price: (v) => v >= 0 }
);

product.price = 49.99; // OK
product.price = -1;   // throws: Invalid value for price: -1
```

## Caching Proxy

```typescript
function createCachingProxy<T extends object>(target: T): T {
  const cache = new Map<string | symbol, unknown>();

  return new Proxy(target, {
    get(obj, prop) {
      if (cache.has(prop)) return cache.get(prop);
      const value = Reflect.get(obj, prop);
      cache.set(prop, value);
      return value;
    },
  });
}
```

## React.lazy — Proxy in the Wild

```typescript
// React.lazy returns a proxy component
// The real component is loaded only when first rendered
const Dashboard = React.lazy(() => import('./Dashboard'));

// <Dashboard /> — Proxy intercepts the first render,
// loads the module, then renders the real component
```

## Use Cases

```
✅ Lazy loading — defer expensive initialisation
✅ Memoisation — cache computed properties
✅ Validation — enforce invariants on object mutation
✅ Logging — track every property access in dev mode
✅ Access control — redact sensitive fields
```

