## Command Pattern

## Intent

Encapsulate a request as a self-contained object — enabling undo/redo, queuing, logging, and decoupling the sender from the receiver.

## Structure

```
Invoker    → sends the command
Command    → encapsulates the action + undo logic
Receiver   → performs the actual work
```

## TypeScript Implementation with Undo

```typescript
interface Command {
  execute(): void;
  undo(): void;
}

// Receiver
class TextEditor {
  private content = '';
  insert(text: string, at: number) {
    this.content = this.content.slice(0, at) + text + this.content.slice(at);
  }
  delete(at: number, length: number) {
    this.content = this.content.slice(0, at) + this.content.slice(at + length);
  }
  getContent() { return this.content; }
}

// Concrete command
class InsertTextCommand implements Command {
  constructor(
    private editor: TextEditor,
    private text: string,
    private position: number
  ) {}

  execute() { this.editor.insert(this.text, this.position); }
  undo()    { this.editor.delete(this.position, this.text.length); }
}

// Invoker — manages history
class CommandHistory {
  private history: Command[] = [];
  private redoStack: Command[] = [];

  execute(command: Command) {
    command.execute();
    this.history.push(command);
    this.redoStack = []; // clear redo on new action
  }

  undo() {
    const command = this.history.pop();
    if (command) { command.undo(); this.redoStack.push(command); }
  }

  redo() {
    const command = this.redoStack.pop();
    if (command) { command.execute(); this.history.push(command); }
  }
}

// Usage
const editor = new TextEditor();
const history = new CommandHistory();

history.execute(new InsertTextCommand(editor, 'Hello', 0));
history.execute(new InsertTextCommand(editor, ' World', 5));
console.log(editor.getContent()); // 'Hello World'

history.undo();
console.log(editor.getContent()); // 'Hello'

history.redo();
console.log(editor.getContent()); // 'Hello World'
```

## Redux as Command Pattern

```typescript
// Redux action = Command object
const addItem = (item: CartItem) => ({ type: 'cart/addItem', payload: item });

// dispatch = Invoker
dispatch(addItem({ id: '1', price: 49.99 }));

// Reducer = Receiver (pure — no undo built in, but actions are logged)
// Redux DevTools time-travel = replaying the command log
```

## When to Use

```
✅ Undo/redo is a requirement
✅ Actions need to be queued, retried, or replayed
✅ You want to log all user actions for audit or debugging
✅ Macro recording (record + replay a sequence of commands)
```

